haiku: Vulkan support in the Haiku video driver

Vulkan has no registered Haiku surface extension; Mesa's Haiku window system
integration takes a BView through VK_EXT_headless_surface, with a
VkHaikuSurfaceCreateInfoMESA (Mesa's <vulkan/vk_haiku_surface.h>) chained to
VkHeadlessSurfaceCreateInfoEXT. This adds:

- SDL_VULKAN for Haiku in CMake (SDL_VIDEO_VULKAN in the Haiku video block);
- SDL_bvulkan.cc: loads libvulkan.so.1 (or SDL_VULKAN_LIBRARY), needs
  VK_KHR_surface + VK_EXT_headless_surface, creates the surface on the
  window's Vulkan view, drawable size = that view's size;
- SDL_BWin: a Vulkan view for SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN windows (made with the
  window, so it is attached before a surface is created; draws nothing, view
  color B_TRANSPARENT_COLOR so app_server does not erase the frames), no GL
  context;
- relative mouse mode set on the window's current view instead of the GL
  view, which a Vulkan or framebuffer window does not have (NULL dereference).

Applied after HaikuPorts' libsdl2-2.32.10.patchset (scripts/cross-port.sh --patches).

